KZ3 patch 2184 (RSX pass 162): LD_WB_READ / LD_WB_SKIP / LD_WB_HASH, measurement switches for the main-memory surface
write-backs (diagnostic, default off). New libs/video/rsx_wb_probe.h (pure core: skip-list parser, per-surface cycle
bookkeeping store -> GETs/PUTs, 64-bit guest hash; host test tools/smoke/test_wb_probe.sh).
- LD_WB_READ=1: [wb-read] line per closed cycle (store k .. store k+1) of every main-memory surface the walker stores:
  store_done_t, first_get_t (ms after the flip that began the store's frame), gets, dirty_gets (GETs that touched bytes no
  SPU PUT had fully overwritten since the store; for 0x01892400 also gets_before_zero), puts, first_put_t, first_walker_t
  and walker_binds (the walker's own first texture bind of the surface after the store), submit_t/wait_ms (start of the
  batch that produced the store; wait = store_done - submit), usercmd_t and gap_ms (the first 0xEB00 queued after the store,
  gcm_walker_user_command, minus submit_t = the walker time a deferred store could hide the GPU wait in), job_pc
  (img<id>:pc of the first GET); [wb-read-sum] every LD_WB_READ_N (default 100) flips: median/min/max slack per surface.
  Feed: new SPU hook g_spu_guest_read_hook2 (spu_dma.h/spu_coherency.c, adds image id and spu->pc to the 2084 GET hook) and
  the 2033 write hook (PUTs); both only installed/used when LD_WB_READ is set.
- LD_WB_SKIP=a,b: ld_writeback_batch drops the surfaces at these main-memory offsets before the copy (no copy, no wait, no
  store); the guest bytes stay stale.
- LD_WB_HASH=1: [wb-hash] hash of the guest bytes of idx0 (0x01310400, 0x384000 B) and idx9 (0x01A62500, 0xE100 B) at the
  first bind per frame (texture_srv_slot_entry); =2 also lists each main-memory texture offset bound.
- idx0 is no surface record: its bytes reach main memory in nv0039_copy after the source surface write-back into guest
  local memory, so nv0039_copy calls rsx_live_draw_wbp_copy_done (copies of >= 64 KB into main memory) after its memmove.

